Third-party material
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following is not ours, and is listed so that anyone reading the code knows
where it came from and on what terms.

TRACKING DATA — not distributed here

  Neither of the two sources publishes a licence file, so no derived tracking
  data is committed to this repository. `play.json` and `soccer.json` are built
  locally from the originals; see tools/README.md for how to fetch them and
  README.md for why. Anyone running this app obtains the source data under the
  terms of whoever published it, directly from them.

    NFL Big Data Bowl (2017 release)
    https://github.com/nfl-football-ops/Big-Data-Bowl

    Metrica Sports open sample data
    https://github.com/metrica-sports/sample-data
    Anonymised at source. Their licence asks that the source be acknowledged,
    which the app does in the replay caption and in the info sheet.

NIGHT SKY TEXTURE — distributed here

    NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Scientific Visualization Studio,
    "Deep Star Maps 2020". Public domain.
    https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4851
    Median-filtered to drop the point stars, which the SDK renders itself,
    and sqrt-encoded so 8 bits keep precision in the dim range.

BRAND ASSETS — referenced, not distributed

    The video board draws an Esri logo fetched at runtime from a public ArcGIS
    Online item. It is a trademark of Esri and is not licensed by this
    repository. Point CONFIG.jumbotron.logo somewhere else for your own build.

RUNTIME SERVICES

    ArcGIS Maps SDK for JavaScript, loaded from js.arcgis.com, under Esri's
    terms of use. https://js.arcgis.com

    Open-Meteo, for live conditions. https://open-meteo.com

    Google Fonts (Fraunces, Inter), under the SIL Open Font License.

THE VENUE

    The scene is a reality capture of a real stadium. Nothing in this app names
    a club, and neither the painted surfaces nor the player kit carries any team
    mark: team names, uniform designs and club marks are trademarks of their
    owners. The playing surfaces are generated by the scripts in tools/.
